  "preamble": "The shift from the lateral approximant [l] to the labiodental [v] is a rare outcome of L-vocalization, which more often gives the labial-velar glide [w] (filed under l → w). In Komi-Zyrian, syllable-final l became v from the 17th century on, as in Proto-Permic *vɔ̇l 'horse' > вӧв vöv and *tul 'nail' > тув tuv.",
